NAME
    impact - compute test units affected by a set of changes

SYNOPSIS
    impact [--base REV] [--head REV] [--tier T] [--depth N]
           [--also TERMS] [--map-age DAYS] [--inputs FILE]
           [--lunap-base REV] [--lunap-head REV] [--repo DIR]
    impact --explain FILE [--tier T] [--depth N] [--inputs FILE]
           [--repo DIR]
    impact --base REV --head REV --blast FILE [--repo DIR]
    impact --base REV --head REV --format blast [--repo DIR]

DESCRIPTION
    Command of the emusen.testing module. Computes the changed files
    between the merge base of --base (default: WiseMan) and --head
    (default: HEAD plus uncommitted working-tree changes), and outputs
    one tab-separated line per selected test unit:

        kind    unit    reason    via

    where kind is 'cargo' or 'dotnet', unit is a crate folder or test
    class (or CLASS#KEY case group), reason is the first matching rule,
    and via is the file that triggered selection. Selection rules, in
    precedence order:

        recording  Changed recording listed in Testing/inputs.json
                   selects its owner (or matching CLASS#KEY group); an
                   unowned recording file closes to the tier's full set.
        always     A test class's own file selects that class; units
                   that failed in the branch's last trial are re-added.
        declared   Matching 'folder' entry in Testing/inputs.json adds
                   its units and narrows reached test projects where all
                   entry crates declare mappings; 'covered:PATHSPEC'
                   adds classes executing those files from the map.
        covered    Changed .cs file present in a fresh coverage map
                   selects classes that executed it (plus any class
                   without a report). Added .cs files select classes
                   covering changed files referencing their types.
        graph      Owner crate/project and its reverse dependency
                   closure (Cargo path deps, workspaces,
                   ProjectReference, Import, and xtask/libraries.tsv).
        closed     Unclaimed file closes to the tier's entire unit set.

    Entries of kind 'none' in Testing/inputs.json claim a file without
    selecting units. Diagnostic notes and stale-map warnings are printed
    to standard error.

OPTIONS
    --base REV
        Base git revision for diffing (default: WiseMan).
    --head REV
        Head git revision (default: HEAD plus uncommitted changes).
    --tier T
        Tier configuration name (default: land).
    --depth N
        Override reverse-closure traversal depth.
    --also TERMS
        Pipe-separated ('|') filter terms adding matching classes with
        reason 'given'.
    --map-age DAYS
        Maximum allowed coverage-map age in days relative to the merge
        base (default: 1.0). Older maps disable the 'covered' rule.
    --inputs FILE
        Read input rules from FILE instead of Testing/inputs.json at
        --head.
    --lunap-base REV
        Diff the sibling LunaP checkout from REV (default: none,
        disabled), injecting changed paths as 'lunap:<path>'.
    --lunap-head REV
        Head revision for the sibling LunaP diff (default: HEAD).
    --explain FILE
        Print FILE's owner, reverse closure, matching input rules, and
        selected units.
    --format blast
        Emit output in blast.sh format ('dotnet filter:', 'cargo:',
        'lunap: selected', and 'closed: FILE' lines).
    --blast FILE
        Compare impact's selection against blast.sh output in FILE
        ('agree', 'impact', or 'blast' per unit).
    --repo DIR
        Git repository root (overrides EMUSEN_REPO).

EXAMPLES
    impact
    impact --base main --head HEAD --tier land
    impact | grep -c '^cargo'
    impact --explain Platform/dianash/src/builtins.rs
    impact --base main --head feature --format blast

EXIT STATUS
    0   Selection computed successfully.
    2   Invalid options, git error, or unreadable input file.

SEE ALSO
    units(1), coverage(1), shard(1), trial(1), results(1)
